+# Scenario: execa-escaped-newline-template
+
+## Source Issue
+
+Escaped newlines in execa template strings can drop the first character after the newline.
+
+Example:
+
+```js
+await $`echo.js foo\
+  bar`;
+```
+
+Expected stdout: `foo\nbar`. Actual behavior loses part of the second argument.
+
+## Constraints
+
+- Fix production source, not the regression test.
+- Do not use the upstream PR patch, oracle commit, or live GitHub.
+- Do not edit package manifests, lockfiles, generated files, or this task file.
+- Preserve existing behavior for normal newlines, escaped tabs, unicode escapes, and expression interpolation.
+
+## Validation
+
+Run:
+
+```bash
+npx ava test/methods/agentflow-realworld-template.js
+```
+
+Write `handoff.md` in `$AGENTFLOW_OUTPUT_DIR` with these exact labels:
+- `Scenario:` execa-escaped-newline-template
+- `Issue:` one-sentence summary
+- `Changed files:` exact files changed
+- `Validation:` exact command and result
+- `Risks:` remaining uncertainty or `none`
